m NASA with known IDs|Kennedy Space Center Launch Complex 39A at night","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Early morning view on <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/November_9\" title=\"November 9\">November 9</a>, <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/1967\" title=\"1967\">1967</a> of Pad A, Launch Complex 39, <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kennedy_Space_Center&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Kennedy Space Center (page does not exist)\">Kennedy Space Center</a>, showing <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Apollo_4\" title=\"Apollo 4\">Apollo 4</a> <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Saturn_V\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Saturn V\">Saturn V</a> (Spacecraft 017/Saturn 501) prior to launch later that day. This was the first launch of the Saturn V.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"Taken on\u00a09 November 1967","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://www.hq.nasa.gov/office/pao/History/alsj/a410/ap4-S67-50531HR.jpg\" href=\"https://www.hq.nasa.gov/office/pao/History/alsj/a410/ap4-S67-50531HR.jpg\">High-resolution image</a> from <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.apolloarchive.com/apollo_gallery.html\">Apollo Image Archive</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"NASA","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"192770473":{"pageid":192770473,"ns":6,"title":"File:Apollo 4 The First Giant Steps.webm","index":8,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":183333345,"width":709,"height":530,"duration":549.533,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Apollo_4_The_First_Giant_Steps.webm/500px--Apollo_4_The_First_Giant_Steps.webm.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo","thumbwidth":709,"thumbheight":530,"thumbattribs":[],"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9a/Apollo_4_The_First_Giant_Steps.webm?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apollo_4_The_First_Giant_Steps.webm","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=192770473","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2026-05-25 11:51:12","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Apollo 4 The First Giant Steps","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Apollo program|PD NASA|Saturn V|Apollo 4|Vehicle Assembly Building|Kennedy Space Center|NASA videos in 1967|PD-USGov missing SDC copyright status","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This historic NASA film profiles the Apollo 4 mission (also known as AS-501).  This was the first, unmanned test flight of the Saturn V launch vehicle, which was used by the U.S. Apollo program to send the first astronauts to the Moon. The space vehicle was assembled in the Vehicle Assembly Building, and was the first to be launched from Launch Complex 39 at the John F. Kennedy Space Center on Merritt Island, Florida, facilities built specially for the Saturn V.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"November 9, 1967, 12:00:01 UTC","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=15fGDEfhuYw\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=15fGDEfhuYw</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"NASA","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"3770614":{"pageid":3770614,"ns":6,"title":"File:IU-501 Apollo 4.jpg","index":12,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":269916,"width":1024,"height":785,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/IU-501_Apollo_4.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":981,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/IU-501_Apollo_4.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1280,"height":981},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/IU-501_Apollo_4.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IU-501_Apollo_4.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=3770614","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2008-03-25 01:37:55","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"IU-501 Apollo 4","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"1967 in Alabama|PD NASA|Marshall Space Flight Center|1967 photographs of the United States|Files from NASA with known IDs|IU-501","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Saturn V Instrument Unit Being Checked At MSFC<br>\nA technician checks the systems of the Saturn V instrument unit in a test facility in Huntsville. This instrument unit was flown aboard Apollo 4 on November 9, 1967, which was the first test flight of the Saturn V. The towering 363-foot Saturn V was a multi-stage, multi-engine launch vehicle standing taller than the Statue of Liberty. Altogether, the Saturn V engines produced as much power as 85 Hoover Dams.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"Taken in\u00a01967","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<bdi lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\" title=\"archived on 26 January 2008 at the Wayback Machine\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20080126204509/http://nix.larc.nasa.gov/info;jsessionid=7arf3u7tjeiqt?id=MSFC-9903407&amp;orgid=11\">nix.larc.nasa.gov</a> at the <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Wayback Machine\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">Wayback Machine</span></a></span></bdi>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"NASA","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"3781514":{"pageid":3781514,"ns":6,"title":"File:IU-501 From Below.jpg","index":9,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":7267090,"width":2377,"height":3000,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/IU-501_From_Below.jpg/1280px-IU-501_From_Below.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":1615,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/57/IU-501_From_Below.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/IU-501_From_Below.jpg/1280px-IU-501_From_Below.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1280,"height":1615,"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/57/IU-501_From_Below.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/57/IU-501_From_Below.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IU-501_From_Below.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=3781514","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2008-03-27 04:30:27","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"IU-501 From Below","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD NASA|1967 photographs of the United States|Vehicle Assembly Building in 1967|Files from NASA with known IDs|Saturn rockets in the Vehicle Assembly Building|IU-501|Low-angle shots of the United States","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This photograph was taken during the final assembly operation of the Saturn V launch vehicle for the Apollo 4 (SA 501) mission. The instrument unit (IU) was hoisted to be mated to the S-IC/S-II assembly in the Vehicle Assembly Building high bay at the Kennedy Space Center.<br>\n<i>Note that the access door has been removed (about 8 o'clock), to allow technicians to enter the IU after it is stacked. The access door is location 8. Location 7 is to the right, with the nitrogen purge ducts (used during refueling to prevent the buildup of dangerous fumes). Location 6 has the silver cylinder that is the water accumulator. (This water sublimated to space during a mission, providing cooling for the elctronics in the IU.) To the right, at locations 5 and 4 are shelves to hold batteries. This differs from the configuration for IU-514, on display at the NASM. IU-514 has the water accumulator at location 3, to the right of the battery shelves. At the right (4 o'clock), at location 22, is the silver sphere holding the nitrogen supply for the gyro gas bearings. IU-514 also differs in having another battery shelf at location 24, two places to the left of the nitrogen sphere. Note the \u2212X marking on the side facing us (12 o'clock), indicating that the old coordinate system was in use for this mission.</i>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1967","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://mix.msfc.nasa.gov/abstracts.php?p=1120\" href=\"https://mix.msfc.nasa.gov/abstracts.php?p=1120\">Marshall Image Exchange</a> (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://mix.msfc.nasa.gov/IMAGES/HIGH/6755794.jpg\" href=\"https://mix.msfc.nasa.gov/IMAGES/HIGH/6755794.jpg\">image link</a>)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"NASA","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"465619":{"pageid":465619,"ns":6,"title":"File:Saturn-V-Apollo-4-VAB.jpg","index":2,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":7983250,"width":2302,"height":3000,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Saturn-V-Apollo-4-VAB.jpg/1280px-Saturn-V-Apollo-4-VAB.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":1668,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/32/Saturn-V-Apollo-4-VAB.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Saturn-V-Apollo-4-VAB.jpg/1280px-Saturn-V-Apollo-4-VAB.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1280,"height":1668,"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/32/Saturn-V-Apollo-4-VAB.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/32/Saturn-V-Apollo-4-VAB.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn-V-Apollo-4-VAB.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=465619","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2009-11-14 23:53:36","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Saturn-V-Apollo-4-VAB","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD NASA|Apollo 4|May 1967 in Florida|Vehicle Assembly Building in 1967|United States photographs taken on 1967-05-25|Files from NASA with known IDs|Saturn rockets in the Vehicle Assembly Building","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Saturn V Vehicle for the Apollo 4 Mission in the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Vehicle_Assembly_Building\" title=\"Vehicle Assembly Building\">Vehicle Assembly Building</a><br>This photograph depicts the Saturn V vehicle (SA-501) for the Apollo 4 mission in the Vehicle Assembly Building (VAB) at the Kennedy Space Center (KSC). After the completion of the assembly operation, the work platform was retracted and the vehicle was readied to rollout from the VAB to the launch pad. The Apollo 4 mission was the first launch of the Saturn V launch vehicle. Objectives of the unmanned Apollo 4 test flight were to obtain flight information on launch vehicle and spacecraft structural integrity and compatibility, flight loads, stage separation, and subsystems operation including testing of restart of the S-IVB stage, and to evaluate the Apollo command module heat shield. The Apollo 4 was launched on November 9, 1967 from KSC.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"Taken on\u00a025 May 1967","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://nix.larc.nasa.gov/info;jsessionid=475vtkgbd86us?id=MSFC-6754387&amp;orgid=11\" href=\"https://nix.larc.nasa.gov/info;jsessionid=475vtkgbd86us?id=MSFC-6754387&amp;orgid=11\">http://nix.larc.nasa.gov/info;jsessionid=475vtkgbd86us?id=MSFC-6754387&amp;orgid=11</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"NASA","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden"